From 9006568472636284f3f137ffa81eff1de8918918 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 04:40:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Jumped list: skip layout and paint of rows off screen

After an A-Z jump the list view leaves the virtual scroller (the start sentinel has to
see real rows), so every loaded page stays in the document. Rows now use
content-visibility: auto with the scroller's 70 px row height, so the browser only lays
out and paints what is near the viewport.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016bdM1DxXcha5BLMHxDaXkJ
---
 src/components/ItemsListing.vue | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/components/ItemsListing.vue b/src/components/ItemsListing.vue
index d431bc1..aa68a45 100644
--- a/src/components/ItemsListing.vue
+++ b/src/components/ItemsListing.vue
@@ -257,7 +257,7 @@
         </v-virtual-scroll>
         <!-- Keep jumped list rows in document flow so the start sentinel can observe
              them and prepending a page has a measurable scroll height. -->
-        <div v-else-if="viewMode == 'list'">
+        <div v-else-if="viewMode == 'list'" class="jumped-list">
           <template
             v-for="(item, index) in listDisplayItems"
             :key="'isDiscHeader' in item ? `disc-${item.disc}-${index}` : item.uri"
@@ -2562,6 +2562,14 @@ defineExpose({
   }
 }
 
+/* A jumped list keeps every page it has loaded in the document, so a long scroll leaves
+   thousands of rows behind; the browser skips laying out and painting the ones off screen.
+   The row height matches the virtual scroller's, so the scroll height stays right. */
+.jumped-list > * {
+  content-visibility: auto;
+  contain-intrinsic-size: auto 70px;
+}
+
 .disc-header {
   display: flex;
   align-items: flex-end;
-- 
